## [:< ##

# name  = plugin.user-edit.key-actions.tab_info
# descr = key-actions plugin's self-description
# param = -none-

## the 'key actions' tab : create a NEW named C25519 key from inside the form
## [ the first interactive key action -- create ONLY, no rename/remove/
## identity-switching ], shown only on the invoking Unix user's OWN record.
##
## pinned_keys => ['key_actions'], DELIBERATELY -- the exact opposite of
## plugin.user-edit.key-details.tab_info's no-pins choice : that tab must
## never be enterable, this one MUST be.  form.handler.stdin_key's Right-entry
## trigger requires BOTH plugin => ... on the field def AND the field's name
## present in the registry's by_key map, and by_key is just a
## string-to-plugin-name map -- it does not care that 'key_actions' is a
## SYNTHESISED field [ pushed directly by form.schema_from_record, carrying
## plugin => 'plugin.user-edit.key-actions' on its own field def ] rather than
## a real record field.  no collision : 'key_actions' appears nowhere in
## users.record.default_fields/.optional_fields.
##
## q|..|, NOT qw|..| : qw splits on WHITESPACE, so qw| key actions | would
## collapse into label => 'key' plus a stray 'actions' key -- the same trap
## plugin.user-edit.key-details.tab_info's own header documents
return {
    qw| label |       => q| key actions |,
    qw| pinned_keys | => [qw| key_actions |],
};

